feature <id> returns that feature's record, including its criteria. feature --code <CODE> returns every feature grouped under that code, and feature with no argument every feature in the corpus. --json writes the matching records as JSON to standard output. An identifier no feature declares is reported as such and exits non-zero. feature <id> --emit writes the named feature as a valid Gherkin .feature file, carrying its tags, description and criteria, to standard output by default and to the path --out names.

Usage:
  specs feature [<id>] [flags]

Flags:
      --code string   list every feature grouped under this code
      --emit          write the feature as a standalone .feature file instead of querying it
  -h, --help          help for feature
      --json          write the matching feature records as JSON to standard output
      --out string    where to write the emitted file: a path, or omitted for standard output

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to the repository's specs.toml (default "specs.toml")
